# F6-32 forensic, timeline B: the same program run with "p" (pageable buffers).
# 8 chunks over 4 streams; per chunk: copy in 10, kernel 10, copy out 10 (model units).
scenario pageable-8-chunks
# A device-to-host copy into pageable memory returns only once the copy has
# completed (installed header), so each one blocks the host thread: hostsync.
csv
stream 1 nonblocking
stream 2 nonblocking
stream 3 nonblocking
stream 4 nonblocking
h2d 1 10 in0
kernel 1 10 k0
d2h 1 10 out0 hostsync
h2d 2 10 in1
kernel 2 10 k1
d2h 2 10 out1 hostsync
h2d 3 10 in2
kernel 3 10 k2
d2h 3 10 out2 hostsync
h2d 4 10 in3
kernel 4 10 k3
d2h 4 10 out3 hostsync
h2d 1 10 in4
kernel 1 10 k4
d2h 1 10 out4 hostsync
h2d 2 10 in5
kernel 2 10 k5
d2h 2 10 out5 hostsync
h2d 3 10 in6
kernel 3 10 k6
d2h 3 10 out6 hostsync
h2d 4 10 in7
kernel 4 10 k7
d2h 4 10 out7 hostsync
end
